# ADR-0005: Swagger UI URL Strategy

## Status

Accepted

## Date

2026-10-08

## Context

The RL Digital API Documentation Platform uses Hugo, Docsy, OpenAPI and Swagger UI to provide interactive API documentation.

OpenAPI specifications are stored as static assets and are consumed by Swagger UI through the `swaggerui` shortcode.

During local development and testing, issues occurred because different deployment environments use different base URLs:

| Environment | Base URL |
|------------|-----------|
| Local Development | http://localhost:1313/rl-digital-api-docs/ |
| GitHub Pages | https://wolfgang61.github.io/rl-digital-api-docs/ |
| Future Hosting Platforms | TBD |

Using hard-coded or root-relative URLs caused Swagger UI to request OpenAPI documents from incorrect locations.

Example:

```text
/openapi/eaapi-v1.yaml
```

This failed when the site was hosted below a context path such as:

```text
/rl-digital-api-docs/
```

---

## Decision

Swagger UI shall always receive URLs generated by Hugo.

The `swaggerui` shortcode shall use:

```go-html-template
url: "{{ $original | absURL }}"
```

OpenAPI specifications shall be referenced without a leading slash.

Example:

```markdown
{{< swaggerui src="openapi/eaapi-v1.